UnitMetaquoter::QuoteRemoveClLiquidityV3
├── when the pool is not a registered target
│   └── it reverts with IP
└── given the pool is a registered target
    ├── when the target factory is not approved
    │   └── it reverts with AF
    └── given the target factory is approved
        ├── when the pool type is not CL
        │   └── it reverts with PT
        └── given the pool type is CL
            ├── when the lower tick is not below the upper tick
            │   └── it reverts with TLU
            ├── when the lower tick is below the minimum tick
            │   └── it reverts with TLM
            ├── when the upper tick is above the maximum tick
            │   └── it reverts with TUM
            ├── when the lower tick is not aligned to the tick spacing
            │   └── it reverts with TS
            ├── when the upper tick is not aligned to the tick spacing
            │   └── it reverts with TS
            └── given the tick range is valid
                ├── when the liquidity is zero
                │   └── it reverts with ILB
                ├── when the liquidity exceeds the int128 maximum
                │   └── it reverts with LTM
                ├── when the liquidity exceeds the gross liquidity at the lower tick
                │   └── it reverts with LS
                ├── when the liquidity exceeds the gross liquidity at the upper tick
                │   └── it reverts with LS
                ├── when the credited token1 amount exceeds the uint128 maximum
                │   └── it reverts with AO
                ├── when the credited token0 amount exceeds the uint128 maximum
                │   └── it reverts with AO
                ├── when the price is inside the range
                │   ├── it returns both amounts rounded down at the live price
                │   └── it returns both sides nonzero
                ├── when the price is below the range
                │   ├── it returns the whole range in token0
                │   └── it returns zero as amount1
                ├── when the price is above the range
                │   ├── it returns the whole range in token1
                │   └── it returns zero as amount0
                ├── when the tick is the lower tick with the price inside it
                │   ├── it returns both amounts rounded down at the live price
                │   └── it returns both sides nonzero
                ├── when the tick is the upper tick with the price inside it
                │   └── it returns zero as amount0
                ├── when the quote is taken at a pinned price and range
                │   └── it returns the amounts the burn would credit
                └── when the liquidity an add quote sized is removed again
                    ├── it returns at most the amounts the add quote required
                    └── it returns amounts within one wei of them
